**Given:**

P can do a piece of work in 48 days

Q can do the same work in 18 days

Q worked at it for 15 days

Calculation:

Work done by P in 1 day = dfrac{1}{48}

Work done by Q in 1 day = dfrac{1}{18}

Work done by Q in 15 days = 15 × dfrac{1}{18} = dfrac{15}{18} = dfrac{5}{6}

Remaining work = 1 - dfrac{5}{6} = dfrac{1}{6}

Time taken by P to complete dfrac{1}{6} of work = dfrac{1}{6} ÷ dfrac{1}{48}

⇒ dfrac{1}{6} × 48 = 8 days

**∴ The correct answer is option (3).**

